{"run_id": "planned-4203-s02-5e5160", "t": 5.869, "type": "model_call", "step": 4, "purpose": "execute", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "latency_s": 0.964, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2728, "output_tokens": 155, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "prompt_tokens": 2728}, "cost_usd": 0.0012059, "tool_calls": [{"name": "tracker_post_comment", "input": {"body": "label: bug\nfile: src/ingest/parser.ts\n\nThe CSV parser handles the Byte Order Mark (BOM) at the start of the text (`if (text.startsWith(BOM)) text = text.slice(BOM.length);`), but `parseStatement` splits lines into `lines` *before* stripping the BOM. When files exported from Windows tools include a leading UTF-8 BOM, `lines[0]` starts with the BOM character (`\ufeffdate,amount,description`), causing header matching and column checks to fail on row 1. Stripping the BOM before splitting into lines will resolve this issue.", "number": 4203}}], "tools": ["tracker_post_comment"], "text": ""}
