{"run_id": "planned-4203-s02-5e5160", "t": 6.841, "type": "tool_call", "step": 5, "plan_step": 6, "name": "tracker_post_comment", "input": {"body": "label: bug\nfile: src/ingest/parser.ts\n\nThe CSV parser handles the Byte Order Mark (BOM) at the start of the text (`if (text.startsWith(BOM)) text = text.slice(BOM.length);`), but `parseStatement` splits lines into `lines` *before* stripping the BOM. When files exported from Windows tools include a leading UTF-8 BOM, `lines[0]` starts with the BOM character (`\ufeffdate,amount,description`), causing header matching and column checks to fail on row 1. Stripping the BOM before splitting into lines will resolve this issue.", "number": 4203}, "is_error": false, "latency_s": 0.002, "result_chars": 31, "result_excerpt": "Posted comment 9 on issue 4203.", "paths": []}
